Z||000000||Eddie||09-24-1999||08:44 PM||||Some ONE told me that if my car had an after market chip. That maybe that is whats turning my exhaust manifold red.Because they tend to dump lots of gas down the exhaust pipe could this be true   ?????||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-24-1999||09:58 PM||||after market chips are available for the V6. A bad one could do this. find a V6 car in a salvage yard and grab the chip. preferably the same or later year, tho any for V6 should do. (Make sure the car has the same tranny as yours. Ie. stick or auto)<P>Warning. if you have a 160 thermostat you will have to put in either a 180 or 195 to run the stock PROM. you don't have to worry about low tamp fan switches.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||09-26-1999||11:23 AM||||No, 85 chips are different than 86-88 for the V6. 6869(85) vs the 7170 ECM (86-88).<P>Still don't know why they add fuel in the chips.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-26-1999||06:47 PM||||they do it because they believe it makes more power. a slightly rich mix can but many are too rich.<P>timing that is retarded cad also be a major problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||09-26-1999||11:03 PM||||I think GM sets the aceleration enrichment slightly lean to avoid a fuel dump when you stab the throttle (to pass Federal emissions). Increasing the FP will improve that and that initial pull from the AE feels better, but when power enrichment kicks in, the car usually pulls worse. We get fooled by the initial AE kick. That's where chip mods really help, but frankly I am unimpressed with many of the chips. I do my own now.||||reg||1
Z||000005||JIM GOOSE||09-27-1999||08:21 AM||||Have you checked your timing?? I had the same deal when I started my motor after having dist. out.  You need to check the initial timing. Running the car in the condition you describe will damage it.||||reg||1
